                          "text":  "In 2006 my right front wheel stopped turning. After that I drove backwards, dragging the dead wheel behind me like a stubborn suitcase. And that is how I made my best discovery. The dragging wheel scraped up bright white soil: nearly pure silica, left behind by ancient hot water or steam. It was a place where tiny living things could once have been comfortable.",
